# 12. Explainable AI

The XAI implementation is in:

- `explain.py`
- `xai_loader.py`

The project uses:

- SHAP
- LIME

## Global SHAP

The global SHAP beeswarm plot shows which features are important across many test records.

This answers:

> Which variables generally influence the model?

It is an aggregate explanation, not a single-patient explanation.

## Temporal SHAP

Temporal SHAP divides ICU time into:

- Early: hours 1–6
- Mid: hours 7–24
- Late: hour 25 onwards

It calculates feature importance separately for each period.

This answers:

> Does the model rely on different features during different stages of ICU stay?

This is an important project contribution because a static model cannot show how feature importance changes over time.

## Representative TP/TN Explanations

The generated waterfall and LIME plots are:

- One representative true-positive case
- One representative true-negative case

They are not explanations for every patient.

They are useful as case studies to demonstrate:

- Why the model correctly flagged a septic case.
- Why the model correctly cleared a non-septic case.

The current dashboard still treats these as representative examples. Truly patient-specific waterfall/LIME image generation is a remaining enhancement.

